  /// Specifies whether the DB instance is publicly accessible. When the DB
  /// cluster is publicly accessible, its Domain Name System (DNS) endpoint
  /// resolves to the private IP address from within the DB cluster's virtual
  /// private cloud (VPC). It resolves to the public IP address from outside
  /// of the DB cluster's VPC. Access to the DB cluster is ultimately
  /// controlled by the security group it uses. That public access isn't
  /// permitted if the security group assigned to the DB cluster doesn't
  /// permit it. When the DB instance isn't publicly accessible, it is an
  /// internal DB instance with a DNS name that resolves to a private IP
  /// address. For more information, see CreateDBInstance .
  pub publicly_accessible: Bool? = None
  pub tags: List[Tag]? = None
  /// A DB subnet group for the DB instance. The new DB instance is created in
