  /// RDS on Outposts, see Working with Amazon RDS on Amazon Web Services
  /// Outposts in the Amazon RDS User Guide . For more information about
  /// CoIPs, see Customer-owned IP addresses in the Amazon Web Services
  /// Outposts User Guide .
  pub enable_customer_owned_ip: Bool? = None
  /// The network type of the DB instance. Valid Values: IPV4 DUAL The network
  /// type is determined by the DBSubnetGroup specified for read replica. A
  /// DBSubnetGroup can support only the IPv4 protocol or the IPv4 and the
  /// IPv6 protocols ( DUAL ). For more information, see Working with a DB
  /// instance in a VPC in the Amazon RDS User Guide.
  pub network_type: Str? = None
  /// The upper limit in gibibytes (GiB) to which Amazon RDS can automatically
  /// scale the storage of the DB instance. For more information about this
  /// setting, including limitations that apply to it, see Managing capacity
  /// automatically with Amazon RDS storage autoscaling in the Amazon RDS User
  /// Guide .
  pub max_allocated_storage: Int? = None
  /// The location where RDS stores automated backups and manual snapshots.
  /// Valid Values: local for Dedicated Local Zones region for Amazon Web
  /// Services Region
  pub backup_target: Str? = None
  /// The instance profile associated with the underlying Amazon EC2 instance
  /// of an RDS Custom DB instance. The instance profile must meet the
  /// following requirements: The profile must exist in your account. The
  /// profile must have an IAM role that Amazon EC2 has permissions to assume.
  /// The instance profile name and the associated IAM role name must start
  /// with the prefix AWSRDSCustom . For the list of permissions required for
  /// the IAM role, see Configure IAM and your VPC in the Amazon RDS User
  /// Guide . This setting is required for RDS Custom DB instances.
  pub custom_iam_instance_profile: Str? = None
  /// The amount of storage (in gibibytes) to allocate initially for the read
  /// replica. Follow the allocation rules specified in CreateDBInstance .
  /// This setting isn't valid for RDS for SQL Server. Be sure to allocate
  /// enough storage for your read replica so that the create operation can
  /// succeed. You can also allocate additional storage for future growth.
  pub allocated_storage: Int? = None
  /// The identifier of the Multi-AZ DB cluster that will act as the source
  /// for the read replica. Each DB cluster can have up to 15 read replicas.
  /// Constraints: Must be the identifier of an existing Multi-AZ DB cluster.
  /// Can't be specified if the SourceDBInstanceIdentifier parameter is also
  /// specified. The specified DB cluster must have automatic backups enabled,
  /// that is, its backup retention period must be greater than 0. The source
  /// DB cluster must be in the same Amazon Web Services Region as the read
  /// replica. Cross-Region replication isn't supported.
  pub source_db_cluster_identifier: Str? = None
  /// Indicates whether the DB instance has a dedicated log volume (DLV)
  /// enabled.
  pub dedicated_log_volume: Bool? = None
  /// Whether to upgrade the storage file system configuration on the read
  /// replica. This option migrates the read replica from the old storage file
  /// system layout to the preferred layout.
  pub upgrade_storage_config: Bool? = None
  /// The CA certificate identifier to use for the read replica's server
  /// certificate. This setting doesn't apply to RDS Custom DB instances. For
  /// more information, see Using SSL/TLS to encrypt a connection to a DB
  /// instance in the Amazon RDS User Guide and Using SSL/TLS to encrypt a
  /// connection to a DB cluster in the Amazon Aurora User Guide .
  pub ca_certificate_identifier: Str? = None
  /// A list of additional storage volumes to create for the DB instance. You
  /// can create up to three additional storage volumes using the names
  /// rdsdbdata2 , rdsdbdata3 , and rdsdbdata4 . Additional storage volumes
  /// are supported for RDS for Oracle and RDS for SQL Server DB instances
  /// only.
  pub additional_storage_volumes: List[AdditionalStorageVolume]? = None
  /// Tags to assign to resources associated with the DB instance. Valid
  /// Values: auto-backup - The DB instance's automated backup.
  pub tag_specifications: List[TagSpecification]? = None
  /// The identifier or the name of the DB capacity reservation to associate
  /// with this read replica. You can specify the identifier, which has the
  /// prefix dbcr- , or the reservation name. When you specify this parameter,
  /// the read replica uses reserved capacity from the specified reservation.
  /// A read replica uses one unit of reserved capacity, in the same way as
  /// any other DB instance. If you specify AvailabilityZone , Amazon RDS
  /// places the DB instance in that Availability Zone, and the reservation
  /// must cover it. Constraints: The reservation must reserve capacity for
  /// the DB instance class and the database engine of the DB instance. If the
  /// reservation reserves capacity for a specific license model, the license
  /// model of the source DB instance must match it. A read replica inherits
  /// its license model from the source DB instance. The reservation must be
  /// in the active state, and it must not be past its end date. If you
  /// specify AvailabilityZone , it must be one of the Availability Zones of
  /// the reservation. For a Multi-AZ DB instance, the reservation must cover
  /// two or more Availability Zones. A Multi-AZ DB instance uses one unit of
  /// reserved capacity in each of two Availability Zones. If the reservation
  /// covers more than two Availability Zones, Amazon RDS chooses the two that
  /// the DB instance uses. The reservation must have available capacity in
  /// each Availability Zone that the DB instance uses. The DB subnet group
  /// must be in a VPC with default tenancy. The DB subnet group must cover
  /// each Availability Zone that the DB instance uses.
  pub db_capacity_reservation_identifier: Str? = None
  /// The region the source lives in: when set and the presigned URL is
  /// not, the SDK presigns this call in that region and sends it as the
  /// presigned URL (as the other AWS SDKs do). Not sent itself.
  pub source_region: Str? = None
}

